# $name

One or two sentences: what is built, from what stock, and where it goes.
Bought-and-cut: the manufacturability layer is a cut plan, screw lengths and
where each number came from. Nothing is printed unless a printed interface
says so.

![render](../../docs/img/$name.png)

## Status

`STATUS` in `params.py` says concept, passes, printed or parked. Here: what
passes and what is open.

## Sources

Standards, vendor sheets and catalogue pages `params.py` cites, and which
values are UNVERIFIED (measure the real stock before cutting).

## Run

```
.venv/bin/python projects/$name/params.py     # prints the design and cut list
.venv/bin/python -m pytest projects/$name
```

